1. GRANT OF LICENSE

Subject to a valid, paid subscription or a signed written agreement with the
Licensor, the Licensor grants the customer ("the Licensee") a non-exclusive,
non-transferable, revocable licence to install and run the Software at the
production sites named in that agreement, for the Licensee's own internal
manufacturing operations.


2. SOURCE AVAILABILITY

The source code is made available to the Licensee so that it can be audited,
validated against the Licensee's own quality procedures, and extended for the
Licensee's internal use. Source availability does not make the Software open
source and does not grant any right beyond those stated in Section 1.


3. PERMITTED

  a. Running the Software on the Licensee's own infrastructure.
  b. Modifying the Software for the Licensee's internal use.
  c. Making backup and disaster-recovery copies.
  d. Auditing the source for regulatory, safety or customer-quality purposes.


4. NOT PERMITTED

Without the Licensor's prior written consent, the Licensee shall not:

  a. Distribute, sublicense, resell, rent or lease the Software, in whole or in
     part, whether modified or unmodified.
  b. Offer the Software, or any derivative of it, to third parties as a hosted
     or managed service.
  c. Remove or obscure any copyright, licence or attribution notice.
  d. Use the Software to build a competing manufacturing execution product.


5. EVALUATION

The Licensor may grant a time-limited evaluation licence in writing. An
evaluation licence permits non-production use only. Running the Software to
control, gate, release or record any saleable product requires a paid licence.


6. NO WARRANTY

THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR
IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,
