7. SAFETY AND FITNESS FOR PURPOSE — READ THIS

The Software records, gates and reports manufacturing process data. It is
NOT a safety system and is NOT certified to any functional-safety standard.

  a. It must never be relied upon as the sole means of preventing injury,
     equipment damage, or the release of a defective product.
  b. Physical safety interlocks, emergency stops, light curtains, guarding and
     safety PLCs remain the Licensee's responsibility and must remain
     independent of the Software.
  c. The Licensee is responsible for validating the Software against its own
     quality management system, and for the correctness of every routing,
     specification limit and interlock it configures.
  d. Nothing in the Software relieves the Licensee of any obligation under
     applicable product-safety, automotive, medical-device or other regulation.


