-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
NOTE TO THE MAINTAINER — DELETE BEFORE PUBLISHING

This is a drafting template, not legal advice, and it has not been reviewed by
a lawyer. Before you take money for this software, have a qualified solicitor
or attorney in your own jurisdiction review Sections 6-10 in particular. The
safety disclaimer in Section 7 is the one you cannot afford to get wrong: you
are selling a system that gates the release of physical product, and a customer
will eventually blame it for an escape. Get that clause right, and carry
professional indemnity / product liability insurance before your first paid
installation.

Also decide deliberately whether you want source-available at all. It is a real
selling point to manufacturers, who distrust black boxes in their quality
systems, but it makes Section 4(d) hard to enforce in practice.
